{
 "esm": "1.1.0",
 "metadata": {
  "name": "RecurrenceSweep",
  "description": "Causal self-reference recurrences (spec \u00a74.5; esm-spec \u00a74.3.1.1) on two (col, lev) states. c: a Thomas solve per column whose diagonal 2 + c\u00b2 reads the state - a forward elimination (bet, a recurrence reading itself through a division), a forward substitution (uf, reading bet) and a back substitution written on the REVERSED lev axis (yrev), so the line block is dense. q: a lag-2 recurrence with a two-cell base guard (p), a linear implicit-trapezoid sweep on a non-uniform axis with a parameter (phi, the entraining-plume shape), a Newton iteration on a non-state axis it (r, read at its last iterate: pointwise), and a filtered window whose filter gathers a const mask (a where guard no box split can express)."
 },
